 #include <cstdlib>
 
-#define GAINZ_MTP_HEAD_N_CAND 98304
+// Candidate rows for the MTP draft head, second cut.
+//
+// 98304 (patch 0003) is where this tokenizer's Latin-and-code region ends,
+// and it was chosen so the reduced head can still propose every token the
+// full projection would have. That is the right bound for "no proposal is
+// ever lost", but it is not the throughput optimum, because a lost proposal
+// costs only ACCEPTANCE while the rows it saves cost BANDWIDTH on every
+// draft step of every verify pass.
+//
+// Priced on this track's own ranked window - benchmarkPrompt(100..108) at
+// 2600 chars, 128 greedy decode steps, cache_prompt off, the median of the
+// server's own timings.predicted_per_second, which is the ranked metric
+// itself - with the shipped MTP depth of 3:
+//
+//     K       decode tok/s   step ms   accepted/pass (median)
+//     98304      47.64         49.04        2.327
+//     32768      48.66         47.79        2.327
+//      8192      45.97         47.24        2.170
+//
+// Both ends reproduce in the reverse arm order (8192: 45.97 / 45.84).
+//
+// The mechanism is visible in the engine's own draft timer: a draft step is
+// 5.30 ms and the whole 3-step draft is 10.8% of the 48.97 ms speculative
+// step, with the LM projection the majority of it. Cutting 98304 -> 32768
+// rows takes the draft to 4.21 ms and the step to 47.79 ms, and the MEDIAN
+// accepted length does not move: the proposals that fall outside 32768 are
+// concentrated in the slices that already accept well, not in the median
+// slice the runner scores. At 8192 the proposal loss finally bites -
+// accepted/pass drops 6.8% and the arm goes negative - which is what fixes
+// the cut here rather than lower.
+//
+// Perplexity is untouched for the same reason it was for the first cut: the
+// MTP block only executes under LLAMA_CONTEXT_TYPE_MTP, and the gate's
+// llama-perplexity runs never create that context type. Batch-1 decode and
+// 512-token prefill run identical kernels either way.
+#define GAINZ_MTP_HEAD_N_CAND 32768
 
 // Vocabulary rows the MTP draft head projects against.
